# A compile over a real process, in a host: the child writes one error line
# and then blocks until it is killed, so the run is the same every time.
# What the host prints holds the working directory's path, which is a
# temporary directory of the run's own, so it is not compared with a file:
# each line of `holds`, beside this script, must be part of a line of it.
#
# The config registers nothing, so every ex name typed is one a package
# compiled into the editor bound. The working directory holds no
# `src/a.rs`.

reload
settle

# `compile` asks for the line, and the answer starts the run: the job
# `compile-run` starts the child under `/bin/sh -c`. The clock is moved
# past the job's pause after its first post, and the scene shows the
# compilation buffer with the header line and the child's line, whose
# location is a span in the face `compilation.error`.
key : Semicolon shift
commit compile
key <Enter> Enter -
commit printf 'src/a.rs:3:5: error: boom\n'; exec sleep 600
key <Enter> Enter -
advance 50
settle
scene

# `kill-compilation` cancels the job, which kills the child, and the last
# line says so.
key : Semicolon shift
commit kill-compilation
key <Enter> Enter -
join
scene

# `next-error` visits the first location: its file is not there, which the
# echo area says with the path resolved against the directory the run ran
# in. The visit loads the file with a job, which `join` waits for: with the
# run killed it is the only job, so the scene is the one after the load's
# refusal, every time. (Before the kill, the run's child is still running,
# and no wait could end at the load alone.)
key : Semicolon shift
commit next-error
key <Enter> Enter -
join
scene

# `previous-error` from the first location has none before it.
key : Semicolon shift
commit previous-error
key <Enter> Enter -
scene

# `recompile` runs the line again with no prompt, in the same buffer,
# emptied: the scene shows the header and the one line again. It is killed
# as the first was, so the script leaves no child.
key : Semicolon shift
commit recompile
key <Enter> Enter -
advance 50
settle
scene
key : Semicolon shift
commit kill-compilation
key <Enter> Enter -
join
scene
